From 40845bba84c673df9d551dd17e898d4698e3237c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brennan Lamoreaux <brennan.lamoreaux@broadcom.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:41:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fips canister plugins: don't compare offsets of pad field

Padding field offset is irrelevant and of course subject to change,
as if a previous field changes in size, the padding field offset may
change. As long as we can resize the pad field to match, and the
offsets of all the other fields are matching between the canister and
the kernel, then everything is hunky-dory.

Signed-off-by: Brennan Lamoreaux <brennan.lamoreaux@broadcom.com>
---
 .../match_canister_structs/match_canister_structs.c             | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/gcc-plugins/fips_canister_plugins/match_canister_structs/match_canister_structs.c b/scripts/gcc-plugins/fips_canister_plugins/match_canister_structs/match_canister_structs.c
index 5a2b4b8b6..5b11a0688 100644
--- a/scripts/gcc-plugins/fips_canister_plugins/match_canister_structs/match_canister_structs.c
+++ b/scripts/gcc-plugins/fips_canister_plugins/match_canister_structs/match_canister_structs.c
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ static int validate_offsets(tree type, struct data_structure *canister_def)
 
 		last_fld_size = get_field_size(field);
 
-		if (!member)
+		if (!member || !strcmp(field_name, PAD_FIELD_NAME))
 			continue;
 
 		if (!strcmp(member->name, field_name) &&
-- 
2.53.0

